index 753ac52..758aaa6 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -80,3 +80,20 @@ Design notes: `docs/TREE_DESIGN.md`. Changes: `CHANGELOG.md`.
 GPL-3.0-or-later (`LICENSE`); it links CommonLibSSE-NG, which is GPL-3.0-or-later. Third-party notices:
 `THIRD_PARTY.md`. Credits: `CREDITS.md`. The release zip carries all three in
 `SKSE/Plugins/EnhancedCombatBehavior/`.
+
+## Local RDF API v2 adaptation (SE 1.5.97)
+
+This branch prefers ReactiveDodgeFramework.dll API v2 over TK events when both are installed.
+ECB supplies a world direction and a probed maximum distance. RDF owns all resource charging, motion,
+clip selection, attack-cancel rules and protection windows. No second ECB stamina charge is applied.
+The old EnableTKDodgeIntegration setting still controls whether NPCs may dodge at all.
+DodgeStaminaCost, IFrameDuration, EnableStepDodge and DodgeEvent* apply only to the TK fallback backend;
+MinDodgeStamina and the forward-dodge stamina percentage remain optional tactical thresholds.
+
+Success accounting and cooldowns wait for RDF's graph-entry confirmation, not queue admission.
+Pending/active RDF dodges suppress further decisions. A refused forward dodge falls back to advancing.
+Requests use handles, can be cancelled while queued, and cannot start later out of RDF's input buffer.
+Without RDF API v2 this fork retains the original TK backend.
+
+Build tested for SE only; this integration still needs in-game verification. It does not extend dodge support
+for humanoid creatures that upstream deliberately excludes. The matching modified RDF DLL is required.
